    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Finalise and publish procurement pack",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN applies to central government departments, their executive agencies and non-departmental public bodies (collectively referred to as ‘in-scope organisations’) when awarding public contracts for goods, and or services, and or works, other than special regime contracts. It is also relevant to other contracting authorities which create, process, store and manage government information.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations must ensure that appropriate protective security controls are in place for new and existing contracts in line with the Government Security Classifications Policy (GSCP).",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The GSCP sets out the administrative system used by HM Government (HMG) to protect information and data assets appropriately against prevalent threats through the use of ‘classification tiers’.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "HMG uses three classification tiers; OFFICIAL, SECRET and TOP SECRET. Each tier provides a set of recommended baseline behaviours and a set of protective controls, which are proportionate to the threat profile for that tier and the potential impact of a compromise, accidental loss or incorrect disclosure of information held within that tier.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Note: This PPN replaces PPN 07/23 for procurements commencing on or after 24 February 2025.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Sensitive information for all new contracts must be handled in accordance with the appropriate security classifications and protections under the GSCP.",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure the procurement and contract documents refer to the appropriate GSCP classifications and are clearly marked, where possible, with a classification tier",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "PPN 012 Security classifications policy",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
